    Attributes
    ----------
    agentEnabled : bool, default is True, optional
        Enable the QEMU guest agent. MUST be true (and the agent
        installed in the template) for the VM IP to be reported
        back onto status.share.ip.

    annotation : str, default is Undefined, optional
        VM description/notes.
    bios : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Firmware — "seabios" or "ovmf".
    bridge : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Network bridge (e.g. vmbr0, vmbrvlan).
    cloneDatastore : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Datastore the CLONE allocates into (clone.datastoreId).
        Unset, Proxmox allocates on the TEMPLATE's datastore and
        bpg then moves the disk to `datastore` — so every build
        writes the full image twice, and the clone needs
        Datastore.AllocateSpace on the template's storage even
        when the VM is not meant to live there. Set this to
        `datastore` to clone straight onto the target.

        OPT-IN ON PURPOSE, and it must stay that way: bpg's
        clone block is ForceNew, so emitting a value where a
        live VM previously rendered none is a spec change on an
        immutable field — the provider would destroy and
        recreate the VM. Existing VMs render byte-identical
        while this is unset.

        `none` is an explicit OPT-OUT: it renders exactly as if
        the field were absent, and it is the ONLY way for an XR
        to decline a value coming from the EnvironmentConfig —
        an empty string is falsy and falls through to it.

        To roll this out for a whole environment: set
        `cloneDatastore: none` on every EXISTING VM's XR first,
        then add the real value to the EnvironmentConfig. New
        VMs pick it up, old ones stay pinned. ORDERING TRAP:
        `none` only means "opt out" from v0.11.0 on — against an
        older package it reads as a datastore literally NAMED
        none, causing the destroy + recreate you are avoiding.
        Bump the package before setting the sentinel anywhere.

    cpu : str, default is "2", optional
        vCPU cores.
    cpuType : str, default is Undefined, optional
