        Changes that need a reboot then wait for the next one.

    tags : [str], default is Undefined, optional
        Proxmox tags for the VM. In LabUL these are the
        assignment mechanism — `se-<kuerzel>` for the person,
        the datastore (`v5010`, `fs9100`), `plb_*` for the
        scheduler — so a VM without them is unattributable.

        MERGED with the EnvironmentConfig's `tags` by default;
        set `tagsPolicy: Replace` to take only what is here.

        Emitted SORTED: the Proxmox API returns tags in
        alphabetical order, so an unsorted list is reported as a
        difference on every reconcile. Duplicates and empty
        entries are dropped for the same reason.

        WHAT IS SET HERE IS THE WHOLE SET ON THE VM. A full
        clone inherits the template's tags (template 144 carries
        `se-phermann;stuttgart-things`, which is why VMs come out
        tagged today without anyone setting this), and the
        provider writes this list over them — it cannot merge
        with what it does not observe (`tags` is absent from
        `status.atProvider`). So a VM that needs an inherited tag
        kept must name it here or on the EnvironmentConfig.
        Leaving this unset changes nothing: no `tags` is emitted
        and the inherited ones stay.

    tagsPolicy : str, default is "Merge", optional
        How `tags` here combines with the EnvironmentConfig's
        `tags`. `Merge` (default) is the union of both; `Replace`
        takes only this XR's list and ignores the environment's.

        `Replace` exists because there is otherwise no way to
        decline an environment-level tag: an empty list is falsy
        in the template and falls straight through to the
        EnvironmentConfig. Same reasoning as the `none` sentinel
        on `cloneDatastore`, and the same caveat — the render has
        no API server, so this default is applied by the
        Composition as well, not only by the XRD.

    templateNode : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Node the TEMPLATE lives on (clone.nodeName), as opposed
        to `node`, which is where the VM RUNS. bpg treats them
        separately — "leave blank, if equal to the node_name
        argument" — and emitting only the target is what forces
        the two to be the same. A template that then moves takes
        every build with it, with an error naming neither:

          unable to find configuration file for VM 211 on node
          'ul-pve01'

        Hit for real after the LabUL rebuild moved the ubuntu26
        templates. Prefer setting it on the EnvironmentConfig:
        where a template lives is a fact about the template, not
        about the VM.

        SAME ROLLOUT TRAP AS cloneDatastore: clone.nodeName is
        ForceNew, so adding this to an EnvironmentConfig rewrites
        the clone block of every EXISTING VM under it — destroy +
        recreate, unattended where compositionUpdatePolicy is
        Automatic. Set `templateNode: none` on the XRs already
        built first, then add the real value to the
        EnvironmentConfig.

    templateVmId : str, default is Undefined, optional
        VMID of the template to clone. bpg clones by numeric
        VMID (not name) — resolve your template (e.g. sthings-u26)
        to its VMID and set it here or, preferably, on the
        EnvironmentConfig.

    vlanTag : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Optional VLAN tag for the NIC.
    vmId : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Optional explicit VMID for the new VM. Omit to let
        Proxmox / the provider assign one.

    """


